{
  "evidence": "TEXT_E: End the NHS internal market, shift money to frontline care, cut cancer waits, create a Patients’ Charter, ban tobacco ads, and set up an independent Food Standards Agency; smaller infant class sizes, universal nursery places, literacy/numeracy targets and lifelong learning; tackle homelessness, revive social housing, a national childcare strategy, parental leave protections, protect Child Benefit and basic pensions; clean‑up politics via a Freedom of Information Act, ECHR incorporation, Lords reform and devolution by referendum; tougher sentencing for serious repeat crime, more police on the beat, victims’ rights and a free vote to ban handguns; economic ‘golden rule,’ more independent monetary policy, no rise in income tax rates, a 10p starting rate, windfall levy to fund welfare‑to‑work, and a sensibly‑set National Minimum Wage via a Low Pay Commission; NATO‑based defence, retain Trident while pursuing multilateral disarmament, and an ethical foreign policy with poverty‑focused aid and climate leadership. TEXT_C: Independence as the route to ‘normal nationhood,’ a written constitution/Bill of Rights, PR parliament and reform of the monarchy; rebuild the NHS as an integrated public service with added funding, tobacco ad ban, dentistry back in the NHS; raise Child Benefit, restore benefits for 16–17s, a pensioners’ package and end means‑testing for residential care; adopt the EU Social Chapter, minimum wage at half median male earnings, remove the NI ceiling for high earners, widen the basic‑rate band; competitive business taxes (cut corporation tax, abolish Class IV NICs), apprenticeships and skills; zero tolerance on petty crime, total handgun ban; withdraw Trident, phased NATO withdrawal, end nuclear reprocessing and accelerate renewables.",
  "reasoning": "Both texts strongly engage Care/Harm and Equality, but TEXT_E marries those with respect for Authority and national Loyalty through constitutional reform within the UK, NATO alignment and measured fiscal ‘golden rule’ proportionality. TEXT_C’s secession, NATO withdrawal and removal of Trident elevate Scottish in‑group loyalty while subverting existing UK authority, making it less aligned with the British electorate’s notable Authority and Loyalty weights despite its robust care/equality offers.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
}
